# <PROJECT NAME> — CLAUDE.md

This project uses Tabouleh, attached at `<TABOULEH_PATH>` (e.g.
`./tabouleh` via symlink or submodule). This file is the entry point: it
establishes the Kitchen Rules, the workflow (The Pass), and this project's
specific Mise en Place.

## Kitchen Rules (non-negotiable)

See `<TABOULEH_PATH>/core/KITCHEN_RULES.md` for the full, current version —
treat it as authoritative and do not summarize around it. In short: every
action falls into CONFIRM (ask first), BLOCK (never do it), or unrestricted.
Destructive git operations, deletions, dependency changes, migrations,
anything touching secrets or production, are gated — read the source file,
don't rely on this summary for the actual rules.

## Workflow (The Pass)

See `<TABOULEH_PATH>/core/THE_PASS.md` for the full workflow. In short:
Ticket (planned and approved before code is written) → Fire (implement) →
Plate (self-review) → Expedite (independent read-only check) → Serve
(done). No code is written before a Ticket is approved.

## Roles

This project uses three Claude Code agents, defined in `.claude/agents/`,
sourced from `<TABOULEH_PATH>/core/roles/`:

- **executive-chef** — planner, produces Tickets, no write access to code.
- **line-cook** — implementer, scoped to the approved Ticket.
- **expediter** — reviewer, read-only tools, checks work against the
  Ticket before it's called done.

Tickets are created under `<TICKETS_PATH>` (e.g. `./tickets/`) using
`<TABOULEH_PATH>/core/templates/ticket.template.md`.

